gage Rates Economy Government Crypto ETFs Personal Finance View All Reviews Best Online Brokers Best Crypto Exchanges Best Savings Rates Best CD Rates Best Money Market Accounts Best Mortgage Rates Best Checking Accounts Best 1-Year CD Rates Best Jumbo CD Rates View All Trade Search Search Please fill out this field. Search Search Please fill out this field. Investing Investing Stocks Cryptocurrency Bonds ETFs Options and Derivatives Commodities Trading Automated Investing Brokers Fundamental Analysis Markets View All Simulator Simulator Login / Portfolio Trade Research My Games Leaderboard Banking Banking Savings Accounts Certificates of Deposit (CDs) Money Market Accounts Checking Accounts View All Personal Finance Personal Finance Budgeting and Saving Personal Loans Insurance Mortgages Credit and Debt Student Loans Taxes Credit Cards Financial Literacy Retirement View All Economy Economy Government and Policy Monetary Policy Fiscal Policy Economics View All News News Markets Companies Earnings CD Rates Mortgage Rates Economy Government Crypto ETFs Personal Finance View All Reviews Reviews Best Online Brokers Best Crypto Exchanges Best Savings Rates Best CD Rates Best Money Market Accounts Best Mortgage Rates Best Checking Accounts Best 1-Year CD Rates Best Jumbo CD Rates View All Financial Terms Newsletter About Us Follow Us News Markets News Markets News, December 4, 2024: Dow, S&P 500, Nasdaq Hit Record Highs as Tech Stocks Soar; Bitcoin Surges Above $100K By Stephen Wisnefski Full Bio Stephen Wisnefski is the Executive Editor of News at Investopedia. He has more than two decades of experience as a journalist and newsroom leader, including 25 years at Dow Jones and The Wall Street Journal. Learn about our editorial policies Updated December 04, 2024 11:51 PM EST Spencer Platt / Getty Images Close Stocks rose to new highs Wednesday, led by big gains for shares of technology companies, while bitcoin surpassed $100,000 for the first time, as a month-long post-election rally shows no signs of fading. The Dow Jones Industrial Average and S&P 500 gained 0.7% and 0.6%, respectively, while the Nasdaq Composite rose 1.3%, as each of the major indexes hit record intraday and closing highs today. Stocks are off to a strong start this month , after posting their biggest monthly gains of the year in November, as investor optimism runs high that the incoming Trump administration will implement pro-growth policies that translate into strong corporate earnings and continued stock market gains. Bitcoin has also surged amid market expectations that the White House and a crypto-friendly Congress will approve measures that support the asset class. Bitcoin was trading at around $103,300 at around 11:15 p.m. ET, up from a low earlier Wednesday of around $95,000. The surge followed news Wednesday afternoon that President-elect Trump named Paul Atkins to lead the Securities and Exchange Commission. Atkins would succeed Gary Gensler, a critic of the crypto industry who last month said he would step down in January. Among the big movers on the stock market Wednesday, Salesforce ( CRM ) shares jumped 11% to lead Dow and S&P 500 gainers, after the cloud software company reported better-than-expected quarterly results and is', timestamp=datetime.datetime(2024, 12, 30, 6, 32, 28, 492554), status='success', summary={'analysis_type': 'general', 'assets': [{'ticker': 'BTC', 'rating': 'Buy', 'target_price': '110,000 - 120,000', 'sentiment': 'Bullish', 'catalysts': ['Pro-crypto policies expected from incoming administration', 'Appointment of Paul Atkins as SEC leader, replacing crypto critic Gary Gensler'], 'kpis': ['Current price: $103,300', 'Recent low: $95,000', 'Price surge: 8.7% in a single day'], 'action': 'Add Long', 'sources': ['Investopedia article by Stephen Wisnefski']}, {'ticker': 'CRM', 'rating': 'Buy', 'sentiment': 'Bullish', 'catalysts': ['Better-than-expected quarterly results'], 'kpis': ['Price increase: 11% on the day'], 'action': 'Add Long', 'sources': ['Investopedia article by Stephen Wisnefski']}], 'sector': {'name': 'Technology', 'sentiment': 'Bullish', 'catalysts': ['Pro-growth policies from incoming administration', 'Strong earnings reports'], 'kpis': ['Nasdaq Composite increase: 1.3%', 'Dow Jones Industrial Average increase: 0.7%', 'S&P 500 increase: 0.6%'], 'top_assets': ['Salesforce (CRM)'], 'recommendation': 'Overweight', 'sources': ['Investopedia article by Stephen Wisnefski']}, 'macro': {'indicators': ['Record highs in major stock indices', 'Bitcoin surpassing $100,000'], 'global_factors': 'Market optimism due to expected pro-growth policies from incoming Trump administration', 'sentiment': 'Risk-on'}}, agent_id='c6c4cc04-8b96-44db-a965-32145f5e03a9', extraction_method='selenium'), WebSearchResult(url='https://www.investors.com/research/best-stocks-sp500-sp400-sp600-magnificent-earnings-growth-december-2024/', title='Access to this page has been denied.', content='Access to this page has been denied. Please verify you are a human Access to this page has been denied because we believe you are using automation tools to browse the website. This may happen as a result of the following: Javascript is disabled or blocked by an extension (ad blockers for example) Your browser does not support cookies Please make sure that Javascript and cookies are enabled on your browser and that you are not blocking them from loading. Reference ID: #99fa993a-c647-11ef-9250-3fd98965ef36 Report an issue Report a problem Experiencing issues with this page? please let us know: You can contact us for assistance. You should use Ref ID : 99fa993a-c647-11ef-9250-3fd98965ef36 You can also send us your feedback: I’m a bot I do not see where to confirm I keep getting the "Please try again" message Other (please elaborate below) Experiencing other issues? Cancel Send ✓ Thank you for the feedback Powered by PerimeterX , Inc.', timestamp=datetime.datetime(2024, 12, 30, 6, 32, 29, 301221), status='success', summary={'analysis_type': 'general', 'assets': []}, agent_id='974b8856-bddf-4fbf-b496-31f761570dde', extraction_method='selenium'), WebSearchResult(url='https://www.ameriprise.com/financial-news-research/insights/q4-2024-market-outlook', title='Q4 2024 market outlook | Ameriprise Financial', content='Q4 2024 market outlook | Ameriprise Financial Skip to main content Skip to footer Q4 market outlook: Will stocks finish the year strong? Anthony Saglimbene, Chief Market Strategist – Ameriprise Financial Oct. 14, 2024 Share chevron_left chevron_right link Copy link Facebook X LinkedIn mail Email chevron_left Stocks climbed to new highs in the third quarter of 2024, bolstered by interest rates cuts and increasing investor optimism that the U.S. economy can avoid a recession. But can stocks keep climbing through year-end? Below, we explore what could keep the momentum in the market going — and what could stand in its way. Here’s our Q3 recap and Q4 outlook: A look back at Q3: Impressive gains in a tough landscape Source: FactSet, data as of Sept. 30, 2024. This example is shown for illustrative purposes only and is not guaranteed. Past performance is not a guarantee of future results. An index is a statistical composite that is not managed. It is not possible to invest directly in an index. Overall, the stock market continued to climb in Q3, although there were a few market surprises along the way. In particular, stocks remained resilient during the month of September, which is historically a more volatile period for equities. Here’s a look back at the highlights: Major U.S. stock averages faced two bouts of volatility, both in July and August. In July, weaker-than-expected jobs data accelerated concerns that U.S. labor trends were slowing more rapidly than many assumed, causing some investors to fear the Federal Reserve might have left interest rates too high for too long. In August, an aggressive unwind of some institutional carry trades, driven by an unexpected rate hike from the Bank of Japan, disrupted global stocks for a brief period. The drawdowns were temporary, with both the Dow Jones Industrial Average and the S&P 500 Index bouncing back quickly and impressively. The S&P 500 Index finished the third quarter higher by +5.5%, notching its fourth consecutive quarter of gains and the seventh positive quarter in the last eight. Overall, the S&P 500 ended September higher by over +20% year-to-date. Notably, the broad-based U.S. stock benchmark finished its best first nine months of the year (in an election year), going all the way back to 1950. Meanwhile, the Dow Jones Industrials Average outperformed the S&P 500 in Q3, rising a healthy +8.2%. The S&P 500 and Dow finished September higher for the fifth straight month, with the S&P 500 logging its first positive September since 2019. More companies outside of tech began to participate in the stock market rally. The NASDAQ Composite rose +2.6% in the third quarter and finished September higher by nearly +22% year-to-date. Although the tech-heavy index performed well heading into the end of September, it was unable to reclaim its early July peak by the end of the third quarter. Interestingly, the narrow leadership of Big Tech, which drove equity markets higher through much of the first half, began to broaden in the third quarter, marked by a shift in stock leadership to cyclical/defensive areas outside of technology, including utilities, real estate, industrials and financials. The Fed’s September rate cut was a bright spot for the market — particularly for small-cap stocks . The Russell 2000 Index rose nearly +9% in Q3, finishing higher by over +12% year-to-date through September. A broadening stock rally, lower interest rates and growing prospects for an economic soft-landing helped increase optimism for small-cap companies in Q3, which have notably trailed their larger-cap/growth-focused peers this year. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 9:04 Loaded : 1.09% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 9:04 1x Playback Rate 2x 1.75x 1.5x 1.25x 1x , selected 0.75x 0.5x Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , s', timestamp=datetime.datetime(2024, 12, 30, 6, 32, 31, 411172), status='success', summary={'analysis_type': 'macro', 'assets': [], 'macro': {'indicators': ['Interest rate cuts', 'U.S. labor trends', 'Global stock volatility', 'S&P 500 and Dow Jones performance'], 'interest_rates': 'Interest rate cuts by the Federal Reserve and unexpected rate hike by the Bank of Japan.', 'global_factors': 'Unexpected rate hike from the Bank of Japan causing global stock volatility.', 'sentiment': 'Bullish'}}, agent_id='e875fa06-bd89-4390-80b4-ed518ae8daf2', extraction_method='selenium')]
