it and Debt Student Loans Taxes Credit Cards Financial Literacy Retirement View All Economy Economy Government and Policy Monetary Policy Fiscal Policy Economics View All News News Markets Companies Earnings CD Rates Mortgage Rates Economy Government Crypto ETFs Personal Finance View All Reviews Reviews Best Online Brokers Best Crypto Exchanges Best Savings Rates Best CD Rates Best Money Market Accounts Best Mortgage Rates Best Checking Accounts Best 1-Year CD Rates Best Jumbo CD Rates View All Financial Terms Newsletter About Us Follow Us News Markets News Markets News, December 4, 2024: Dow, S&P 500, Nasdaq Hit Record Highs as Tech Stocks Soar; Bitcoin Surges Above $100K By Stephen Wisnefski Full Bio Stephen Wisnefski is the Executive Editor of News at Investopedia. He has more than two decades of experience as a journalist and newsroom leader, including 25 years at Dow Jones and The Wall Street Journal. Learn about our editorial policies Updated December 04, 2024 11:51 PM EST Spencer Platt / Getty Images Close Stocks rose to new highs Wednesday, led by big gains for shares of technology companies, while bitcoin surpassed $100,000 for the first time, as a month-long post-election rally shows no signs of fading. The Dow Jones Industrial Average and S&P 500 gained 0.7% and 0.6%, respectively, while the Nasdaq Composite rose 1.3%, as each of the major indexes hit record intraday and closing highs today. Stocks are off to a strong start this month , after posting their biggest monthly gains of the year in November, as investor optimism runs high that the incoming Trump administration will implement pro-growth policies that translate into strong corporate earnings and continued stock market gains. Bitcoin has also surged amid market expectations that the White House and a crypto-friendly Congress will approve measures that support the asset class. Bitcoin was trading at around $103,300 at around 11:15 p.m. ET, up from a low earlier Wednesday of around $95,000. The surge followed news Wednesday afternoon that President-elect Trump named Paul Atkins to lead the Securities and Exchange Commission. Atkins would succeed Gary Gensler, a critic of the crypto industry who last month said he would step down in January. Among the big movers on the stock market Wednesday, Salesforce ( CRM ) shares jumped 11% to lead Dow and S&P 500 gainers, after the cloud software company reported better-than-expected quarterly results and is', 'timestamp': '2024-12-30T06:32:42.614067', 'status': 'success', 'summary': {'summary': '', 'key_points': [], 'market_impact': {'short_term': '', 'medium_term': '', 'long_term': ''}, 'trading_implications': {'entry_points': [], 'exit_targets': [], 'stop_loss_levels': [], 'position_sizing': ''}, 'technical_analysis': {'trend_direction': '', 'support_levels': [], 'resistance_levels': [], 'indicators': {}}, 'sentiment_analysis': {'overall_sentiment': '', 'sentiment_score': '', 'social_metrics': {'social_volume': '', 'sentiment_trend': ''}, 'market_confidence': ''}, 'risk_assessment': {'risk_level': '', 'risk_factors': [], 'mitigation_strategies': [], 'risk_reward_ratio': ''}, 'price_analysis': {'current_price': '', 'target_prices': {'short_term': [], 'medium_term': [], 'long_term': []}, 'price_drivers': [], 'volatility_assessment': ''}}, 'agent_id': 'c6c4cc04-8b96-44db-a965-32145f5e03a9', 'extraction_method': 'selenium'}, {'url': 'https://www.investors.com/research/best-stocks-sp500-sp400-sp600-magnificent-earnings-growth-december-2024/', 'title': 'Access to this page has been denied.', 'content': 'Access to this page has been denied. Please verify you are a human Access to this page has been denied because we believe you are using automation tools to browse the website. This may happen as a result of the following: Javascript is disabled or blocked by an extension (ad blockers for example) Your browser does not support cookies Please make sure that Javascript and cookies are enabled on your browser and that you are not